Consider the following code running in main.dart:
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
void main() => runApp(const MaterialApp(
home: Scaffold(
body: Center(
child: Text('Hello, World',
style: TextStyle(fontSize: 28, fontWeight: FontWeight.bold)),
),
),
));
If the `const` keyword before `MaterialApp` is removed, what happens to the app's behavior?

Consider:
dynamic x = 10;
x = "Hello";
print(x);
What happens when this code runs?

Given:
List<int> nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
var result = nums.map((e) => e * 2).where((e) => e > 4).toList();
print(result);
What is printed?

Consider this named constructor code:
class Point {
int x, y;
Point(this.x, this.y);
Point.origin() : x = 0, y = 0;
}
void main() {
var p1 = Point(3, 4);
var p2 = Point.origin();
print('${p1.x},${p1.y} - ${p2.x},${p2.y}');
}
What is printed?

Given:
String? name;
print(name ?? "Guest");
name = "Minh";
print(name!.length);
What is printed, in order?

In the following code, what is printed to the console?
void main() {
try {
int result = 10 ~/ 0;
print(result);
} catch (e) {
print("Error: $e");
} finally {
print("Done");
}
}

Given this function:
void greet({String name = "Guest", int age = 18}) {
print("$name is $age");
}
What does calling `greet(name: "Lan");` print?

Consider this OOP code:
class Animal {
String sound() => "Some sound";
}
class Dog extends Animal {
@override
String sound() => "Woof";
}
void main() {
Animal a = Dog();
print(a.sound());
}
What is printed, and which OOP concept does it illustrate?

Consider this code illustrating Dart's Event Loop:
import 'dart:async';
void main() {
print("A");
scheduleMicrotask(() => print("micro"));
Future(() => print("future"));
print("B");
}
What is the correct output order?

Given this Stream code:
Stream<int> countUp() async {
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
yield i;
}
}
void main() async {
await for (var value in countUp()) {
print(value);
}
}
What is printed?

Given this string interpolation code:
String name = "FPT University";
print("Hello $name");
print("Length: ${name.length}");
print("Upper: ${name.toUpperCase()[0]}");
What character does the third line print?

Consider this code, predict the result:
Future<String> fetchData() async {
await Future.delayed(Duration(seconds: 1));
return "Data loaded";
}
void main() {
print("Start");
fetchData().then((value) => print(value));
print("End");
}
What order is printed to console?

Consider the Student class and mini-lab:
class Student {
String name;
Student(this.name);
}
void main() async {
var list = [Student("An"), Student("Binh")];
await Future.delayed(Duration(seconds: 1));
list.forEach((s) => print(s.name));
}
If the `await` keyword before `Future.delayed(...)` is removed, what happens?
